   "title": "DFM Foods sale: EQT, Emami, Balaji Wafers join ITC, TPG in ₹5,500 crore race",
   "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"
  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Swedish private equity firm EQT Partners, Emami Ltd, and Balaji Wafers have joined ITC, TPG, and ChrysCapital in the race to acquire Crax snacks owner DFM Foods. Advent International is seeking to sell its entire 96.63% holding in the Noida-based snack maker. Non-binding bids are expected by the end of October, with the deal potentially valuing the target at Rs 5,000 to 5,500 crore, and Advent expects to close the sale process by December. Balaji Wafers' founder and managing director Chandu Virani confirmed the negotiations, stating they are exploring the possibility of buying into DFM Foods. Advent International has mandated Avendus Capital and EY to advise on the transaction.",
